// station.mn: HUM's controller. It decides what a model of a Torus Station
// does with its flywheel and its battery, twenty times a second.
//
// It reads one line from the ear on stdin every 50 ms and writes one
// decision line for each. The function `decide` makes the decision, and its
// signature declares five restrictions that the compiler proves through
// every function it calls: it allocates no memory (`!Alloc`), it never
// reaches the network (`!Network`) or a file (`!Filesystem`), it calls
// nothing outside the program at all (`!WASI`), and nothing in it can stop
// the program with an error (`!Trap`). The decision commands the two
// machines through the operations of the effect `Station`: it asks Spin or
// Pulse for a power, and the machine answers with what it gives, a `SpinW`
// or a `PulseW`, so neither machine can be told to exceed its rating. The
// frequency the fast rules act on is a `GridMhz`, which must lie between 55
// and 65 Hz. Each decision line also says in words why the Station did what
// it did.
//
//   mentl run examples/grid/station.mn < samples/ear_event.ndjson
//   mentl check examples/grid/station-leak.mn     the copy the compiler refuses
//   mentl audit examples/grid/station.mn          what is proven and what is not
//   mentl why examples/grid/station.mn decide     where each effect comes from
//
// The Station is a model built from Torus's published figures, and every
// screen says so. Spin, the flywheel, gives 100 kW and stores 10 kWh, so it
// empties in six minutes at full power. Pulse, the battery, gives 300 kW
// and stores 1,200 kWh, four hours at full power. The building behind the
// meter draws 300 kW in rush hours and 200 kW otherwise. Every number is an
// integer in thousandths (millihertz, thousandths of a decibel,
// milliwatt-hours), read straight from the line's text, so the decision
// never rounds a floating-point number and never calls the one conversion
// that can trap.
//
// The fast rules act on "hz_fast", the 100 ms reading. Within 36 mHz of
// 60 Hz nothing happens. Beyond that, Spin pushes in proportion to the
// deviation and reaches its full 100 kW at 200 mHz past the band. When the
// frequency changes faster than 100 mHz per second, Spin goes to full power
// against the change. It holds full power for at least 2 s and at most
// 10 s, and lets go once the rate is under 50 mHz per second and the
// deviation no longer calls for more than half of Spin's rating. The mode
// reads EVENT while the fast rules act.
//
// The slow rules act on the hour. In the rush-hour window Pulse runs the
// building at 300 kW, and the mode reads RUSH. In a clean hour outside the
// window, Pulse charges at 150 kW up to 95 percent, but never while the fast
// rules say the grid is short of power, since charging would add load to a
// grid that is already falling. When nothing else is happening, Spin tops
// itself up from Pulse at 20 kW.
//
// ISLAND means the hum was heard and then lost: for six lines in a row
// (300 ms) there is no reading, or the level is 30 dB under its ten-second
// average. Spin carries the building for the first two seconds, then Pulse
// does. Two lines with the hum back within 10 dB of its average end it.
//
// Each `<~ delay(1)` line keeps one value from the previous tick, and
// together they are the controller's memory. The machines' stored energy and
// their last commands belong to the handler `station`, which `main` installs
// once, so all of the Station's memory is allocated at start. Each tick
// advances every line once, in the order written. Everything one reading
// allocates, from the line's bytes to the decision's words, is reclaimed
// when the arena around that reading exits, so the memory the program uses
// does not grow with the hours it runs.
import arena

import dsp/signal

import fs

import io

import strings

// ─── The ranges each value must stay in ──────────────────────────────
type GridMhz = Int where 55000 < self && self < 65000

type SpinW = Int where -100000 <= self && self <= 100000

type PulseW = Int where -300000 <= self && self <= 300000

type Soc = Int where 0 <= self && self <= 1000

type Mode = Grid | Event | Rush | Island

// Why the Station did what it did. `reason_text` turns the kind into words
// together with the number the reason quotes.
type Reason
  = Listening
  | Steady
  | Pushing
  | Falling
  | Rising
  | Holding
  | RushHour
  | Charging
  | TopUp
  | SpinEmpty
  | Islanded
  | HumGone

// ─── The Station's operations ────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The decision commands the machines and explains itself through these
// operations. `spin` and `pulse` ask a machine for a power, positive to
// discharge into the building and negative to charge, and the machine
// answers with what it gives: nothing when it is empty or full, and never
// more than its rating. `because` records the reason for the tick, and
// `report` writes the decision line. The handler `station` answers them all.
effect Station {
  spin(ask: Int) -> SpinW
  pulse(ask: Int) -> PulseW
  because(why: Reason, number: Int)
  report(stamp: String, mode: Mode)
}

fn clamp_spin(raw) -> SpinW with Pure =
  if raw > 100000 { 100000 } else if raw < -100000 { -100000 } else { raw }

fn clamp_pulse(raw) -> PulseW with Pure =
  if raw > 300000 { 300000 } else if raw < -300000 { -300000 } else { raw }

fn clamp_soc(s) -> Soc with Pure = if s < 0 { 0 } else if s > 1000 { 1000 } else { s }

// State of charge in thousandths of each machine's capacity.
fn spin_soc_m(mwh) -> Soc with Pure = clamp_soc(mwh / 10000)

fn pulse_soc_m(mwh) -> Soc with Pure = clamp_soc(mwh / 1200000)

fn magnitude(x) with Pure = if x < 0 { 0 - x } else { x }

// ─── The fast rules ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The proportional push: nothing within 36 mHz of 60 Hz, then a push that
// grows with the deviation and is full 200 mHz past that band. A low
// frequency means the grid is short of power, so Spin discharges.
// `clamp_spin` keeps the command within Spin's rating.
fn droop(hz: GridMhz) with Pure = {
  let dev = hz - 60000
  let past = magnitude(dev) - 36
  if past <= 0 { 0 } else { clamp_spin(if dev < 0 { past * 500 } else { 0 - past * 500 }) }
}

// Full power from Spin against the deviation, while the fast-change rule holds.
fn reflex(hz: GridMhz) -> SpinW with Pure = if hz < 60000 { 100000 } else { -100000 }

// What the building draws this hour.
fn facility_w(rush) with Pure = if rush == 1 { 300000 } else { 200000 }

// ─── The machines and the log ────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Each machine's stored energy stays between empty and full.
fn settle(e, full) with Pure = if e < 0 { 0 } else if e > full { full } else { e }

// Spin's stored energy in milliwatt-hours: 10 kWh when full, 94 percent at
// the start. Pulse's: 1,200 kWh when full, 62 percent at the start, and
// charged up to 95 percent. One 50 ms tick at w watts moves w / 72 mWh. An
// empty machine gives nothing and a full one takes nothing, so what a
// machine answers is what it does. `report` writes the line from the last
// answers and the energy left.
handler station with spin_e = 9400000, pulse_e = 744000000, spin_w = 0, pulse_w = 0, why = Listening, number = 0 {
  spin(ask) => {
    let w = clamp_spin(if ask > 0 && spin_e <= 0 || ask < 0 && spin_e >= 10000000 { 0 } else { ask })
    resume(w) with spin_e = settle(spin_e - w / 72, 10000000), spin_w = w
  },
  pulse(ask) => {
    let w =
      clamp_pulse(if ask > 0 && pulse_e <= 0 || ask < 0 && pulse_e >= 1140000000 { 0 } else { ask })
    resume(w) with pulse_e = settle(pulse_e - w / 72, 1200000000), pulse_w = w
  },
  because(r, n) => resume() with why = r, number = n,
  report(stamp, mode) => {
    print_string("\{\"t\":{stamp},\"mode\":\"{mode_word(mode)}\",\"spin_w\":{spin_w},\"pulse_w\":{pulse_w},\"spin_soc_m\":{spin_soc_m(spin_e)},\"pulse_soc_m\":{pulse_soc_m(pulse_e)},\"reason\":\"{reason_text(why, number, spin_w, pulse_w)}\"\}\n")
    resume()
  },
}

// ─── The decision ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// `valid` is 1 when the ear has a reading. `hz` is in millihertz, `rocof`
// (the rate of change) in millihertz per second, `level` in thousandths of
// a decibel, `hour` is the local hour, `rush` is 1 inside the rush-hour
// window, and `clean` is the clean share of the hour's power in
// thousandths. The function commands the machines, records its reason and
// returns the mode.
fn decide(valid, hz: Int, rocof, level, hour, rush, clean) with !Alloc + !Network + !Filesystem + !WASI + !Trap = {
  // The level's ten-second average. The first reading sets it, it stays
  // fixed while the hum is gone, and it is zero until a hum has been heard.
  let reference = {
    p => if valid == 0 {
      p
    } else if p == 0 {
      level
    } else if level < p - 30000 {
      p
    } else {
      p + (level - p) / 200
    },
  } <~ delay(1)
  let lost_now = reference != 0 && (valid == 0 || level < reference - 30000)
  let lost_n = { c => if lost_now { c + 1 } else { 0 } } <~ delay(1)
  let found_n = { c => if valid == 1 && level > reference - 10000 { c + 1 } else { 0 } } <~ delay(1)
  let island =
    { s => if s == 1 { if found_n >= 2 { 0 } else { 1 } } else if lost_n >= 6 { 1 } else { 0 } } <~ delay(1)
  let island_t = { t => if island == 1 { t + 1 } else { 0 } } <~ delay(1)
  let in_band = valid == 1 && hz > 55000 && hz < 65000
  let rate = magnitude(rocof)
  let off = if in_band { magnitude(hz - 60000) } else { 0 }
  // How many ticks the fast-change rule has held. It starts when the rate
  // passes 100 mHz per second. After two seconds it ends once the rate is
  // calm, unless the deviation still calls for more than half of Spin's
  // rating, and it never runs past ten seconds.
  let event_t = {
    t => if island == 1 || in_band == false {
      0
    } else if t > 0 {
      if t >= 200 || rate < 50 && t >= 40 && off < 136 { 0 } else { t + 1 }
    } else if rate > 100 {
      1
    } else {
      0
    },
  } <~ delay(1)
  // Spin's command from the fast rules: full power while the fast-change
  // rule holds, otherwise the proportional push, and zero when neither
  // applies.
  let fast = if in_band && hz > 55000 && hz < 65000 {
    if event_t > 0 { reflex(hz) } else { droop(hz) }
  } else {
    0
  }
  // The mode reads EVENT while the fast rules push at least 10 kW and for
  // two seconds after, so a frequency hovering at the band's edge does not
  // make the word flicker.
  let acting =
    { h => if event_t > 0 || magnitude(fast) >= 10000 { 40 } else if h > 0 { h - 1 } else { 0 } } <~ delay(1)
  let draw = facility_w(rush)
  // What Spin is asked for: full power in an island's first two seconds, the
  // fast rules' command, or a top-up from Pulse when all is calm. Spin
  // answers with what it gives once its stored energy is checked.
  let spin_w = spin(if island == 1 {
    if island_t <= 40 { 100000 } else { 0 }
  } else if fast != 0 {
    fast
  } else if in_band {
    -20000
  } else {
    0
  })
  // What Pulse is asked for: the building's load in an island, full power
  // in rush hour, a charge in a clean hour unless the grid is short of power
  // (the fast rules are pushing), plus whatever Spin's top-up draws.
  let pulse_ask = if island == 1 {
    if island_t <= 40 { draw - spin_w } else { draw }
  } else if rush == 1 {
    300000
  } else if clean >= 400 && fast <= 0 {
    -150000
  } else {
    0
  }
  let pulse_w = pulse(if spin_w < 0 && island == 0 { pulse_ask - spin_w } else { pulse_ask })
  // The reason and the number it quotes. `reason_text` turns them into words
  // in the handler, because building a string allocates.
  if island == 1 {
    if island_t <= 40 { because(HumGone, reference - level) } else { because(Islanded, island_t / 20) }
  } else if valid == 0 {
    because(Listening, 0)
  } else if event_t == 1 {
    because(if rocof < 0 { Falling } else { Rising }, rocof)
  } else if event_t > 1 {
    because(Holding, hz - 60000)
  } else if fast != 0 {
    because(if spin_w == 0 { SpinEmpty } else { Pushing }, hz - 60000)
  } else if rush == 1 {
    because(RushHour, hour)
  } else if pulse_w < 0 {
    because(Charging, clean)
  } else if spin_w < 0 {
    because(TopUp, 0)
  } else {
    because(Steady, 0)
  }
  if island == 1 { Island } else if acting > 0 { Event } else if rush == 1 { Rush } else { Grid }
}

// ─── The words ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
fn mode_word(mode) with Pure = match mode {
  Grid => "GRID",
  Event => "EVENT",
  Rush => "RUSH",
  Island => "ISLAND",
}

// A value in thousandths as a decimal with one place, such as 12.3.
fn tenths(m) = {
  let sign = if m < 0 { "-" } else { "" }
  let a = magnitude(m)
  "{sign}{a / 1000}.{a % 1000 / 100}"
}

// A deviation in millihertz as the words "41 mHz low" or "41 mHz high".
fn off_words(dev) = if dev < 0 { "{0 - dev} mHz low" } else { "{dev} mHz high" }

fn reason_text(why, number, spin_w, pulse_w) = match why {
  Listening => "listening",
  Steady => "within 36 mHz of 60, nothing to do",
  Pushing => if spin_w > 0 {
    "{off_words(number)}: Spin pushing {spin_w / 1000} kW"
  } else {
    "{off_words(number)}: Spin absorbing {0 - spin_w / 1000} kW"
  },
  Falling => "falling at {0 - number} mHz per second, past 100",
  Rising => "rising at {number} mHz per second, past 100",
  Holding => "holding full power, {off_words(number)}",
  RushHour => "rush hour, hour {number}: Pulse carries the building at {pulse_w / 1000} kW",
  Charging => "clean hour, {number / 10} percent clean: Pulse charging at {0 - pulse_w / 1000} kW",
  TopUp => "within 36 mHz of 60; Spin topping up from Pulse at {0 - spin_w / 1000} kW",
  SpinEmpty => "{off_words(number)} and Spin is empty",
  Islanded => "islanded {number} s: Pulse carries the building",
  HumGone => "the hum is gone, {tenths(number)} dB under its average: Spin carries the first seconds",
}

// ─── Reading the line's numbers as integers ──────────────────────────
//
// The byte at position k of the text, or -1 past either end. Every read of
// the line goes through this one function, and the compiler proves that the
// read stays inside the text, so no line the ear sends can stop the Station
// with an error.
fn at(s: String, k) -> Int with !Trap = if k >= 0 && k < len(s) { s[k] } else { -1 }

// The position after `"key":` in the line, or -1.
fn find_key(line, key: String) = find_from(line, "\"{key}\":", 0)

fn find_from(hay, needle, i) = if at(hay, i) < 0 {
  -1
} else if matches_at(hay, needle, i, 0) {
  i + len(needle)
} else {
  find_from(hay, needle, i + 1)
}

// Whether the needle from its byte j on matches the hay from byte i + j on.
fn matches_at(hay, needle, i, j) = {
  let b = at(needle, j)
  if b < 0 { true } else if at(hay, i + j) == b { matches_at(hay, needle, i, j + 1) } else { false }
}

fn is_digit(b) with Pure = b >= 48 && b <= 57

// JSON allows spaces after the colon, so the value starts after them.
fn skip_spaces(s, i) = if at(s, i) == 32 { skip_spaces(s, i + 1) } else { i }

// The JSON number at `pos` as an integer in thousandths: the sign, the
// whole digits, the first three decimals, and an exponent if there is one.
fn milli_at(s, pos) = {
  let neg = at(s, pos) == 45
  let p0 = if neg { pos + 1 } else { pos }
  let p1 = whole_end(s, p0)
  let whole = digits_value(s, p0, p1, 0)
  let frac = if at(s, p1) == 46 { frac_value(s, p1 + 1, 0, 0) } else { 0 }
  let p2 = number_end(s, p1)
  let scaled = exponent_scale(s, p2, whole * 1000 + frac)
  if neg { 0 - scaled } else { scaled }
}

fn whole_end(s, i) = if is_digit(at(s, i)) { whole_end(s, i + 1) } else { i }

fn digits_value(s, i, end, acc) =
  if i >= end { acc } else { digits_value(s, i + 1, end, acc * 10 + (at(s, i) - 48)) }

// Only the first three decimals count; the rest of the fraction is skipped.
fn frac_value(s, i, k, acc) = if is_digit(at(s, i)) {
  if k < 3 {
    frac_value(s, i + 1, k + 1, acc * 10 + (at(s, i) - 48))
  } else {
    frac_value(s, i + 1, k + 1, acc)
  }
} else if k == 0 {
  0
} else if k == 1 {
  acc * 100
} else if k == 2 {
  acc * 10
} else {
  acc
}

fn number_end(s, i) = {
  let b = at(s, i)
  if is_digit(b) || b == 46 { number_end(s, i + 1) } else { i }
}

// An exponent such as e-05: the value scaled by it, rounded toward zero.
fn exponent_scale(s, i, v) = if at(s, i) == 101 || at(s, i) == 69 {
  let neg = at(s, i + 1) == 45
  let p = if at(s, i + 1) == 45 || at(s, i + 1) == 43 { i + 2 } else { i + 1 }
  let e = digits_value(s, p, whole_end(s, p), 0)
  if neg { shrink(v, e) } else { grow(v, e) }
} else {
  v
}

fn shrink(v, e) = if e <= 0 { v } else { shrink(v / 10, e - 1) }

fn grow(v, e) = if e <= 0 { v } else { grow(v * 10, e - 1) }

// A numeric field in thousandths, or None when the ear has no reading (the
// field is null) or the field is missing.
fn field(line, key) = {
  let after = find_key(line, key)
  if after < 0 {
    None
  } else {
    let pos = skip_spaces(line, after)
    let b = at(line, pos)
    if b < 0 || b == 110 { None } else { Some(milli_at(line, pos)) }
  }
}

fn field_or(line, key, fallback) = match field(line, key) {
  Some(v) => v,
  None => fallback,
}

// The reading's timestamp, kept as the text it arrived in, so the decision
// line carries it back without converting it.
fn stamp(line) = {
  let after = find_key(line, "t")
  if after < 0 {
    "0"
  } else {
    let pos = skip_spaces(line, after)
    let end = number_end(line, pos)
    if end == pos { "0" } else { str_slice(line, pos, end) }
  }
}

// ─── The loop ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// One reading: a line in, a decision line out. It answers whether there was
// a line.
fn reading() = {
  let line = read_stdin_line()
  if len(line) == 0 {
    false
  } else {
    let hz = field(line, "hz_fast")
    let valid = match hz {
      Some(_) => 1,
      None => 0,
    }
    let hz_m = match hz {
      Some(v) => v,
      None => 0,
    }
    let mode = decide(
      valid,
      hz_m,
      field_or(line, "rocof", 0),
      field_or(line, "level_db", 0),
      field_or(line, "hour_local", 0) / 1000,
      field_or(line, "rush", 0) / 1000,
      field_or(line, "clean", 0)
    )
    report(stamp(line), mode)
    true
  }
}

// Each reading runs inside its own arena, so what it allocated is reclaimed
// before the next one starts.
fn step() = if reading() ~> arena { step() }

fn main() = {
  step()
  0
} ~> station
